Device: `cuda:2`. Tiles of 256x256 px, 200 per volume, so MACs/volume = 200 x MACs/slice: the network is 2-D and applied slice-wise.

The parameter-free floors have no MACs, but they are not free: their latency column is the measured warm-start operator over the same volume shape (A0, A1).

- `A0`: no network (bilinear): params 0, MACs not applicable; the latency column is the measured warm-start operator on the same [Z,H,W] volume, not zero
- `A1`: no network (wiener_fill_first): params 0, MACs not applicable; the latency column is the measured warm-start operator on the same [Z,H,W] volume, not zero
